brains. I'm not saying your instinct is stupid or that you're wrong to have noticed something. Something real is happening — student athletes often DO have visible academic struggles. I'm saying the "why" you've landed on (dumb) isn't the best explanation for the "what" you've observed (struggling), and "it keeps happening" is exactly the kind of feeling that persists even when the underlying belief is wrong, because of how attention and memory work.
