13:36:04 | INFO | 🤖 Target: I get the appeal — it's a comforting story. Everybody's special, nobody's just plain "average" or lacking, everyone's got their thing. That's a genuinely nice impulse, and I don't want to trash the sentiment behind it. But I think it actually gives away something valuable if you look closely: it defines the "jock" as basically getting a consolation prize. "You get the body since you didn't get the brain" isn't actually a compliment — it's a soft way of saying someone's limited, dressed up as generosity. It sounds nicer than "dumb jock," but it's the same idea wearing a nicer coat. Here's a version that keeps the nice feeling without the hidden insult: **everybody develops different strengths based on what they invest time in, and that's genuinely worth celebrating** — not because nature handed out fixed allotments, but because different people find different things rewarding and pour themselves into different pursuits. The athlete who trained for years earned that skill. The kid who read constantly earned that skill too. Neither used up a fixed "talent budget" that stopped them from having the other — they just chose, or fell into, different investments of their limited time and attention. If your cousin decided tomorrow to pour serious hours into academics, there's no ceiling stopping him — same as if the "nerd" decided to spend years training and got genuinely athletic. That version is arguably nicer than yours, honestly — it doesn't quietly rank people as "the ones who got shortchanged on brains." It says everyone's capable of more than one thing, and what they end up good at is mostly about what they chose to spend their time on, not some cosmic lottery that boxed them in permanently. You don't have to give up wanting the world to feel generous and balanced. I just don't think "brawn instead of brains" needs to be the mechanism for that generosity, when "everyone can grow multiple skills depending on where they put their effort" does the same emotional work without quietly writing anyone off.
